{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observer Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observer Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observer pattern observer pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observer Pattern.md","fileName":"Observer Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observer Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Object-Oriented Design Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observer Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observer Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observer pattern observer pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observer Pattern.md","fileName":"Observer Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observer Pattern","heading":"Observer Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The observer pattern lets a subject notify registered observers when its state changes, without knowing the observers' concrete types. The book's C# subject raises an event after inventory quantity changes, and several observer objects subscribe through matching delegates. The subject remains loosely coupled to its consumers; subscription and unsubscription define who receives each update.\n\nObserver reverses repeated polling by letting the subject retain a set of interested observers and notify them when relevant state changes. C# events and delegates provide language mechanisms for implementing this publisher-subscriber relationship.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"page